WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:05.238 line:0%
-Ashley, your family just made
a list of things at a gym.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.574 line:0%
-Hmm.
-Time to start guessing.

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:08.975 line:0%
-Dumbbells.

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:12.144 line:0%
-Whoo-hoo-hoo!

00:00:12.144 --> 00:00:13.379 line:0%
-Juice-heads.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.948 line:0%
-I'm so sorry, Ashley.

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:18.117
-[ Laughing ] Juice-heads.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:19.986
-That's a brain freeze.
[ Alarm blaring ]

00:00:23.222 --> 00:00:25.191
-Oh, come on!

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:28.528
Oh! Oh!

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.497
Oh, my gosh!

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:32.898
-[ Screams ]

00:00:32.898 --> 00:00:34.534
-Oh!

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.903
How about when it goes
in your crack, huh?

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.037
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:39.939
We're here with Kristen Bell
and Dax Shepard.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:42.207
So, "Family Game Fight!" --
it's very fun,

00:00:42.207 --> 00:00:43.943
because you have families
competing against each other,

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:46.845
but then, you guys
actually compete, as well,

00:00:46.845 --> 00:00:49.248
which I think makes it
a lot more enjoyable to watch,

00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:51.250
because this show -- and don't
take this the wrong way --

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.053
seems a little mean.

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:56.389
-Thank you so much.
-It's the meanest show there is.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.924
-We hate this show.
-It's a bad, bad show.

00:00:58.924 --> 00:01:01.994
-It's cruel. It's --

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:04.864
-It's rude.
-There's malice.

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.634
-What kind of show --
Because that "Brain Freeze" game

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:10.870
you just saw, it's not just ice
being dumped on your head.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:15.141
They hook us up to a tube,
to the inside of our shirt.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.443
So it goes --
Ice goes right on your skin.

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:19.778
That's why --
I mean, it's brutal!

00:01:19.778 --> 00:01:21.614
There's pies to the face.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:24.417
There was a trampoline game
when we came in,

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.252
and we're like,
"Wait, we're guessing clues,

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.220
but we have to be
jumping on the trampoline?"

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.823
And our producers
are like, "Yeah."

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:32.092
-And we both get nauseous
within two jumps.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:34.260
-They go,
"Well, if you puke, you puke."

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.396
And we were like,
"What did we sign up for?"

00:01:37.396 --> 00:01:40.466
But we didn't really
look at the games.

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:42.234
-Life's moving fast, Seth.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:43.803
You just kind of wake up on set

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:45.605
and you learn
you're gonna have --

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.641
In that game,
we played six times in a row,

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:51.211
so 18 buckets of ice
on the head.

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:52.745
And --
-It's not cute. It's not nice.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.113
-No. But --

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:56.382
-Do you think the families --
I'm sorry to interrupt,

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.184
but do you think the families
ever look at you

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.019
and think, "We know why
we're doing this,

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.921
but why are you doing this?"

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.089
-Sure.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:04.857
-I think it's 50/50.
Yeah, it's polarizing.

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:06.392
There's like half
that would say that,

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.828
like, "You guys
really are silly."

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:09.896
-"You're really flushing
your careers down the toilet,

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:11.064
aren't you?"

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.332
-We heard a bit of --
The murmurs of that.

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:14.900
And then,
other people that are like,

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.102
"Oh, they're kind of cool

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.204
because they are not going to
win any money,

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.405
and here they are with us."

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:22.008
So, you know,
it can go either way.

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:24.544
-I also want to
ask about this before we go.

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:26.279
Kristen,
you have an animated show

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.180
that you are doing called
"Do, Re &amp; Mi."

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:29.582
This is for younger kids.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.684
This is maybe the kind of show

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.285
that my children could watch.

00:02:33.285 --> 00:02:35.822
-This show could have kept you
safely indoors, Seth.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.090
-That's true.
-Oh, thank God, yeah.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.892
-So, yeah, two of my friends
and I got together.

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:41.327
They had this great idea.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:44.897
As music and art was being
slashed from public schools --

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:45.965
And still is.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.867
And that's been happening
for 20 years.

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:50.537
How music was so
formidable in my life.

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:53.372
It brought me here right now, if
I hadn't had a love for music.

00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:54.641
It also proves, you know,

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:56.576
expanding their
brains in math and social.

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.377
We were like, "How do we get
a music education

00:02:58.377 --> 00:02:59.746
into a kid's life?"

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:02.381
And Amazon made
this great show with us.

00:03:02.381 --> 00:03:04.650
It's about three little
songbirds, Do, Re, and Mi,

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.787
and everything about
the show is entertainment,

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:10.890
but it's also secretly teaching
your kid music theory

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.825
about different types of music,
cultural music,

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.026
how to make music.

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:16.862
And we'll have "games"
that go along with it,

00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:18.364
because the kids
love to play it.

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.032
But if they're on it,
they're actually learning

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:22.535
how to interact with music,
make their own music,

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.237
cooperation, all these good
things for brain development.

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:25.471
-It's subversive.
-It's very subversive.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.705
-Subversive.

00:03:26.705 --> 00:03:29.175
-And it's -- Yeah,
really, really proud of it.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.477
-Dax, will you be
a voice on this show?

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:33.345
-I will not.
I will not do that, Seth.

00:03:33.345 --> 00:03:34.514
-It's a singing show.

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:37.817
-It's to teach people
about harmony and notes,

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:38.884
all things I can't accomplish.

00:03:38.884 --> 00:03:40.153
-Gotcha.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:42.187
-But if we need a car-engine
noise, we will call you.

00:03:42.187 --> 00:03:44.891
-Or like the singers want to
point at some guy like,

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:47.793
"Ah, he sounds terrible" --
that could be me.

00:03:47.793 --> 00:03:50.729
-That's nice of you offering
a way to participate.

00:03:50.729 --> 00:03:52.999
You guys, it is always so
lovely to see you.

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:54.433
Thank you for
being here in person.

00:03:54.433 --> 00:03:55.801
It was a delight.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:59.638
-Well, it's our pleasure.
We owed you at least this much.

00:03:59.638 --> 00:04:02.041
-"Family Game Fight!"

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.377
airs on Wednesday at 9:00 p.m.
here on NBC,

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:07.112
and "Do, Re &amp; Mi"
will be on Amazon Prime Video

00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:08.881
and Amazon Kids+
on September 17th.

